"""Mutations of part 8d-iv's volumetrics and clouds (src/game/volumetrics.*) for ../mutfast.py with
the world build:

    python mutfast.py mutations/mutate_8d4.py --models DIR --build build_world.bat --check check_world.py

DIR holds a .txt per mission ("mission NAME"; the tests run the same in each). Each mutation should
make check_world.py fail (or the harness crash / hang). Generated from the 8d-iv lines (a
comparison, a number, an operator or a statement per line), then pruned. Left out as equivalent
(73):
- Directions only read for their sign or normalized again: the shared normalization's unit test
  (1.5, sq + 1), its threshold, a short vector's unit forms dropped, the camera's ground
  direction's unit test and scale, the y parts of the ground directions (0 or multiplied by 0),
  the clouds' direction before SetDir (which normalizes).
- Exact ties that cannot occur or give the same: segments at the room's end, the fades' bounds
  (the same fade or none either way), the cloud fade's bands, alpha at 0 or 1, counts / 4.
- Not read: the cones' initial vertices and coordinates (Build writes them first), a stale chunk
  id, a destructor's nulling, the list's unknown +0x14 and initial direction (atan2 of 0, 0 is
  the same), Draw's w clearing (the world matrix has 0 there), Draw's return values that cannot
  be reached (a fade of exactly 0 at the bounds), the fade -1 as -1.5.
- Leaks or the chunk's destructor: the clouds' buffers' delete, Load's Ascend / Close for another
  version; the 263-character name buffer's size (a fix); the lattice's outer cells (always beyond
  the fade); the clouds' Identity (SetDir sets the rotation, the translation is set after).
- Layout only: the room for 11 segments, the list's destructor.
6 more did not compile and were dropped.

Run 1 (442): 298 caught, 138 survived, 6 not built. New cases for 67: chunks cut short and
left before the next one; cones without a light; two segments; a cone's fade of 0 and 0.3; a fan
rendered twice; Draw's matrix with the camera beside the light; the camera off the origin and
turning, diagonal, tilted, up and short; shafts sideways, slightly ahead, at the fade's end, at
equal distances and next to the camera; the clouds compared vertex by vertex (the camera 3 m
before a cloud, other cells' scales, short directions). Draw's clouds and states in Render.
DrawClouds takes the (unused) time again. Run 2 (365): 359 caught; 4 more cases.
The full rerun (363): all caught.
"""
